# Per-domain generator flags; see linkml/GAPS.md S3.
#
# --xsd-anyuri-as-iri is deliberately OFF. It is an ASCS-eV fork feature whose
# purpose is to make gen-owl and gen-jsonld-context agree with gen-shacl's
# sh:nodeKind sh:IRI. This repository wants the opposite for manifest:filePath
# and manifest:iri: the hand-written shapes and the instance data both treat
# them as xsd:anyURI LITERALS (51 explicit "@type": "xsd:anyURI" declarations
# across tests/data), and filePath holds relative paths that must not be
# resolved against a document base.
#
# With the flag off, gen-owl emits owl:DatatypeProperty + rdfs:range xsd:anyURI
# and gen-jsonld-context emits "@type": "xsd:anyURI" - both correct. gen-shacl
# has no such flag and still emits sh:nodeKind sh:IRI, so it is the only
# generator out of step. See linkml/GAPS.md D5.
OWL_EXTRA_FLAGS=""
SHACL_EXTRA_FLAGS=""
CONTEXT_EXTRA_FLAGS=""
